---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const phone = '+16105550199';
const phoneDisplay = '(610) 555-0199';
---
<Layout title="HVAC Repair in Phoenixville, PA | Same-Day Service" description="Fast, licensed HVAC repair in Phoenixville, PA. Same-day AC, furnace & heat pump service, upfront pricing, and workmanship guarantee. Serving Chester County.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero-badge">● PHOENIXVILLE & CHESTER COUNTY · 24 / 7 EMERGENCY SERVICE</div>
      <h1>HVAC REPAIR IN PHOENIXVILLE</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">Fast Fixes. Real Relief. Same-Day Service. When your AC or furnace fails in Phoenixville, every uncomfortable hour counts. Our licensed technicians are on call around the clock.</p>
      <div class="hero-ctas">
        <a href={`tel:${phone}`} class="btn btn-primary">Call Now — {phoneDisplay}</a>
        <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-outline">Request a Quote</a>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-trust">
        <span>⏱ Same-Day Response</span>
        <span>🛡 Licensed & Insured</span>
        <span>✓ Upfront Pricing</span>
        <span>📞 24 / 7 Emergency</span>
        <span>🛡 Workmanship Guarantee</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">Why Phoenixville Homeowners Choose Us</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">Phoenixville homes need reliable heating and cooling year-round. When your system struggles, you need a licensed local specialist who responds the same day and repairs it right the first time.</p>
      <div class="grid-4">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon">⚡</div>
          <h3>Same-Day Diagnosis & Repair</h3>
          <p>Most same-day HVAC repair calls in Phoenixville are completed within hours of your call — no multi-day waits.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon">📜</div>
          <h3>Licensed & Certified</h3>
          <p>Every technician is licensed, insured, and trained on AC, furnace, heat pump, and hybrid systems common in Chester County.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon">💵</div>
          <h3>Upfront Pricing, Zero Surprises</h3>
          <p>We quote before we wrench. No hidden fees, no upsell pressure — just honest HVAC repair at fair local rates.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon">📍</div>
          <h3>Local to Phoenixville</h3>
          <p>Based in Phoenixville — we know the housing stock, common brands (Carrier, Trane, Lennox, Rheem), and local climate demands.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="stats">
        <div class="stat"><div class="stat-num">47 min</div><div class="stat-label">Avg. Response</div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="stat-num">98%</div><div class="stat-label">First-Visit Fix Rate</div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="stat-num">24/7</div><div class="stat-label">Emergency Available</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">Recognize These Signs?</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">Age, humidity, and Pennsylvania seasons accelerate HVAC wear. If your system shows any of these symptoms, don't wait.</p>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <div class="card">
          <span class="badge badge-urgent">Urgent</span>
          <h3>No Cooling</h3>
          <p>Complete loss of cool air often means a failed compressor, refrigerant leak, or electrical issue. Same-day service restores comfort fast.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="badge badge-urgent">Urgent</span>
          <h3>No Heat</h3>
          <p>Furnace or heat pump failure leaves your home cold. Act quickly in winter — we diagnose and repair the same day in most cases.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="badge badge-soon">Address Soon</span>
          <h3>Strange Noises</h3>
          <p>Banging, screeching, or rattling usually means worn bearings, loose parts, or failing motors. Early service prevents bigger failures.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="badge badge-soon">Address Soon</span>
          <h3>High Energy Bills</h3>
          <p>Sudden spikes often point to dirty coils, low refrigerant, or failing components working harder than they should.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="badge badge-urgent">Urgent</span>
          <h3>Poor Airflow</h3>
          <p>Weak vents can signal clogged filters, duct issues, or a failing blower. Comfort and air quality suffer quickly.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="badge badge-soon">Address Soon</span>
          <h3>Thermostat Issues</h3>
          <p>System short-cycling or ignoring setpoints is often a thermostat, sensor, or control board problem — usually a quick fix.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">Expert HVAC Repair Services</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">Every comfort problem has a root cause. Our certified technicians diagnose accurately and repair correctly.</p>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <div class="card">
          <span class="badge badge-urgent">Urgent Response</span>
          <h3>Emergency HVAC Repair</h3>
          <p>When heating or cooling fails at the worst moment, we respond around the clock — no after-hours surcharge surprises.</p>
          <ul style="margin:0.75rem 0;padding-left:1.1rem;list-style:disc;color:var(--text-muted);font-size:0.9rem">
            <li>Available 24 / 7</li>
            <li>Avg. response under 60 min</li>
            <li>Stocked service vehicles</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="/services/emergency-hvac-repair/" class="card-link">Learn More →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="badge badge-soon">Most Common</span>
          <h3>AC Repair</h3>
          <p>Central air, ductless mini-splits, and heat pumps. Compressors, capacitors, refrigerant, and full diagnostics for all major brands.</p>
          <ul style="margin:0.75rem 0;padding-left:1.1rem;list-style:disc;color:var(--text-muted);font-size:0.9rem">
            <li>All major brands</li>
            <li>Written estimate first</li>
            <li>Same-visit repairs</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="/services/ac-repair/" class="card-link">Learn More →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="badge badge-soon">Winter Essential</span>
          <h3>Furnace Repair</h3>
          <p>Gas and electric furnaces. Ignitors, flame sensors, inducer motors, and heat exchangers — honest repair vs replace advice.</p>
          <ul style="margin:0.75rem 0;padding-left:1.1rem;list-style:disc;color:var(--text-muted);font-size:0.9rem">
            <li>Gas & electric</li>
            <li>Safety inspections</li>
            <li>Same-day when possible</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="/services/furnace-repair/" class="card-link">Learn More →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Heat Pump Repair</h3>
          <p>Year-round comfort systems. Defrost cycles, reversing valves, and dual-fuel setups common in the Philadelphia suburbs.</p>
          <a href="/services/heat-pump-repair/" class="card-link">Learn More →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>HVAC Maintenance</h3>
          <p>Seasonal tune-ups, filter changes, coil cleaning, and safety checks that extend equipment life and lower energy use.</p>
          <a href="/services/hvac-maintenance/" class="card-link">Learn More →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>HVAC Installation</h3>
          <p>Code-compliant AC, furnace, and heat pump installs with proper sizing for Phoenixville homes and local climate.</p>
          <a href="/services/hvac-installation/" class="card-link">Learn More →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">How We Restore Your Comfort</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">Every Phoenixville HVAC repair follows a structured, transparent process.</p>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step">
          <div>
            <h3>Scheduling & Same-Day Response</h3>
            <p>Call or text. We confirm your appointment quickly — often offering same-day slots. We gather a brief symptom overview so the technician arrives prepared.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div>
            <h3>Precision Diagnostic Inspection</h3>
            <p>We test electrical components, refrigerant levels, airflow, heat exchangers, and controls. Problems are identified with instruments, not assumptions.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div>
            <h3>Honest Findings & Repair Options</h3>
            <p>Before any work begins, your technician explains exactly what was found in plain language. You receive a clear written estimate. No pressure.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div>
            <h3>Skilled Repair</h3>
            <p>With your approval, the repair begins. Service vehicles carry common parts so most jobs finish on the first visit.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div>
            <h3>Performance Verification</h3>
            <p>We verify temperature output, check for leaks, confirm thermostat response, and leave you with a post-repair summary.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">Find Us in Phoenixville, PA</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">Proudly serving Phoenixville and all of Chester County from Gay Street.</p>
      <div class="grid-2" style="align-items:start">
        <div>
          <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.75rem">📍 25 Gay St, Phoenixville, PA 19460</h3>
          <p style="color:var(--text-muted);margin-bottom:1rem">Serving Phoenixville · Spring City · Royersford · Collegeville · Malvern · King of Prussia · West Chester · Pottstown and surrounding communities.</p>
          <a href={`tel:${phone}`} class="btn btn-primary">Call {phoneDisplay}</a>
        </div>
        <div class="map-wrap">
          <iframe title="Map of 25 Gay St, Phoenixville PA" src="https://www.openstreetmap.org/export/embed.html?bbox=-75.5249%2C40.1204%2C-75.5049%2C40.1404&amp;layer=mapnik&amp;marker=40.1304%2C-75.5149" loading="lazy"></iframe>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="cta-banner">
        <h2>HVAC Down in Phoenixville?</h2>
        <p>Don't suffer through a hot or cold house. If your system stopped working, is making unusual sounds, or running inefficiently — our team can respond today.</p>
        <a href={`tel:${phone}`} class="btn btn-primary">Call Now — {phoneDisplay}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">HVAC Repair Questions</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">Real answers to what Phoenixville homeowners ask most.</p>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>My AC stopped producing cool air — is this an emergency?</h3>
        <p>Yes, especially with kids, elderly residents, or medical needs. Most complete failures trace to a capacitor, contactor, refrigerant issue, or electrical fault. Emergency calls placed earlier in the day are typically completed same-day.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>How much does HVAC repair cost in Phoenixville?</h3>
        <p>Simple fixes (capacitor, contactor, thermostat) often range from a few hundred dollars. We provide a written estimate before any work begins. Replacement is recommended when the unit is old and repair exceeds roughly 50% of replacement cost.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Do you repair both AC and furnaces?</h3>
        <p>Yes. We service central air, ductless mini-splits, gas and electric furnaces, heat pumps, and hybrid systems from all major brands including Carrier, Trane, Lennox, Rheem, Goodman, and more.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Are you licensed and insured in Pennsylvania?</h3>
        <p>Yes. All work is performed by licensed, insured technicians familiar with Pennsylvania mechanical codes and best practices for HVAC systems in Phoenixville and Chester County.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Should I repair or replace my HVAC system?</h3>
        <p>Repair usually makes sense if the unit is under 10–12 years old and the issue is isolated. Replacement is worth evaluating for units 12+ years old, recurring failures, or when repair cost approaches half the value of a new system. We give an honest assessment either way.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
